{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1299793-aquatic-martial-arts-equivalents","id":1299793,"title":"Aquatic Martial Arts Equivalents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-25T17:38:41-07:00","id":1299793,"title":"Aquatic Martial Arts Equivalents","content":"I'm fiddling with running an all aquatic campaign. In addition to coming up with diverse peoples and nations, I'm working on what Martial Arts Styles work best for that aspect of the setting, and what adjustments may be necessary...<br /> <br /> <b>Snake Style</b> is largely the same (understood as emulating sea snakes)<br /> Tiger Style becomes <b>Siaka Style</b> with some tweaks to use bites more than slashes<br /> Falcon Style becomes <b>Dolphin Style</b>, using a lot more upward swoops rather than downward<br /> Mantis Style becomes <b>Crab Style</b><br /> Centipede Style become <b>Octopus Style</b>, with at least Chitinous Centipede Shell needing to be completely replaced<br /> Silver Voiced Nightingale Style becomes <b>Deep Singing Whale Style</b> - requires some sort of adaptation to actually vocalize underwater (the echolocation Merit is one example), as the dominant language the characters will use is sign based<br /> We haven't seen Bear Style yet, but with its savage grappling it may be a good fit to adjust into <b>Kraken Style</b><br /> <b>Ebon Shadow Style</b> can pretty much stay as is, as does <b>Steel Devil Style</b><br /> <br /> I'm thinking most other surface styles (at least those we know) have not been picked up by subaquatic peoples. But I'm open to other suggestions, and if anyone has any ideas for distinct aquatic styles truly invented beneath the sea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-25-2019, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T18:31:39-07:00","id":1299808,"title":"","content":"I'm imagining Single Point Shining into the Void style as focusing on the way it disrupts water and generates churn. Each slash is accompanied by a whirl of water that disrupts the enemies defenses before it hits, only to be sealed away when the sword is sheathed.<br /> Crane Style is ... Anemone Style?<br /> <br /> As for original aquatic styles<br /> Some kind of cephalopod style trying to mimic color shifting and mimicry.<br /> Turtle Style potentially as a very defensive style, but it probably needs some additional hook.<br /> Anglerfish Style (don't know what it does). Form charm literally gives you a glowy thing floating in front of your head. Possibly anima based<br /> Jellyfish Style - maybe something passive and counterattacky with lots of poison? I guess this could be crane style if you tilt your head a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T19:26:55-07:00","id":1299819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1299793-aquatic-martial-arts-equivalents?p=1299808#post1299808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm imagining Single Point Shining into the Void style as focusing on the way it disrupts water and generates churn. Each slash is accompanied by a whirl of water that disrupts the enemies defenses before it hits, only to be sealed away when the sword is sheathed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mantis Shrimp Style?<br /> <br /> I really don't see sword styles being usable underwater, though. At least not ones that rely on the edge of the blade and swift slashing motions. I'd think you'd want weapon styles based on jabbing and thrusting at opponents and puncturing them to minimize water resistance... probably using spears, tridents, and maybe rapier-like blades.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 03-25-2019, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T21:24:36-07:00","id":1299852,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve gotta figure Water Dragob can just stay as is. Maybe Wood Dragon becomes Swaying Seaweed Style, I think air dragon is right out, and earth would be too dependant on fighting at the sea floor. Fire dragon you could perhaps do something with aquatic thermal vents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T21:27:56-07:00","id":1299854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1299793-aquatic-martial-arts-equivalents?p=1299852#post1299852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve gotta figure Water Dragob can just stay as is. Maybe Wood Dragon becomes Swaying Seaweed Style, I think air dragon is right out, and earth would be too dependant on fighting at the sea floor. Fire dragon you could perhaps do something with aquatic thermal vents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just lean toward the Immaculate Styles having not been adapted. Let it be a deadly weapon of the Water Aspect DBs from the surface world that aquatic civilizations haven\u2019t had teachers for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T21:53:04-07:00","id":1299857,"title":"","content":"I hope that <b>Black Claw</b> becomes <b>Sexy Merman Style ~</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}